        "body": "After a season that ended in the 8th spot of the Atlantic with 78 points, the Toronto Maple Leafs are no longer dwelling on the past but aggressively rebuilding for the future. <strong>No. 1 overall draft pick Gavin McKenna has officially joined the roster</strong>, signaling a fresh era under GM John Chayka, who insists a GM's job is to \"star-hunt.\" The Leafs have already added Sergei Bobrovsky, Jack Roslovic, Colton Sissons, and Brandon Duhaime, reshaping their depth and cap flexibility while trading Nick Robertson and Dennis Hildeby to clear space. McKenna's \"IQ is off the charts,\" according to Dr. Hayley Wickenheiser, and he's even willing to give up his draft number 72 for Bobrovsky's legacy. <strong>What to watch next is whether the Leafs target Kane as the ideal fit alongside their new additions</strong> to push the Atlantic Division title race.",
